{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794262497745566002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"confident-snooty-stinkpot","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"13947a28836e2dc9e42a4b4a0311a1a076b541440fd51940e9e8dddf978653cf","event_uuid":"4f151d33-0abd-4a0f-8255-9f3affe54538","position":{"commit_sha":"7f4bf6ba3942ebf96b646165909d18812746d755","position":"1794255883375978001-4f151d33-0abd-4a0f-8255-9f3affe54538"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"2a5278390d156e13239fe2d8437ab213063b9d0bf5e4fd8b07d06e825655f7fa","event_uuid":"9a57c356-a20a-40fa-b981-81fa74203a4d","position":{"commit_sha":"bd570c8b96d598ceaba9b2d90efd08ba9a7866f5","position":"1794256207633381001-9a57c356-a20a-40fa-b981-81fa74203a4d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"a1699e783a41b2b80b468a37fdf5983414a65bbed4f6aa5f36d84b1f6a554923","event_uuid":"c64a6c84-2f31-49ab-a0f2-e33321b5db5a","position":{"commit_sha":"38528e01a9040f3924a93efea3e2b9288d9d6a89","position":"1794257454419832001-c64a6c84-2f31-49ab-a0f2-e33321b5db5a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"2d9916a271c6a0730e98adaa9b4f569e065516e316971fcca9d1cc7d97658e45","event_uuid":"7ea8e375-b1a3-4ad6-9321-3dae241fd5b1","position":{"commit_sha":"bd2e93f5b9dfc631016f5a4b0153546e7c485503","position":"1794260861496032001-7ea8e375-b1a3-4ad6-9321-3dae241fd5b1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"94851cd4733de1dfa3dc016143d756191a1af527563867ab2ff902a5662a0919","event_uuid":"9f3d73e7-7961-4cc7-a801-3ef2896413de","position":{"commit_sha":"a79e10c39d25df4ca6e0d00b0d2364a0b7b6d7b3","position":"1794262497745566001-9f3d73e7-7961-4cc7-a801-3ef2896413de"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794255883375978001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9a57c356-a20a-40fa-b981-81fa74203a4d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2473-79b7-1048-4a71"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nBoth engines must produce the same verdict contract, so downstream readers (claim gate, `review-plan --status`, `sign-review`, MCP status tools, the sidecar readers) need no change and the two engines are directly comparable. The pipeline's verdict is built by `orchestrator.finalize_verdict` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py:333`) and recorded by `sidecar.build_payload`/`sidecar.emit` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py:586`, `:58`) against `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_verdict.schema.json` and `review_result.schema.json`. The agentic engine returns a different finding shape.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd an adapter in the agentic module's package (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic_verdict.py`) that maps agentic findings onto the pipeline's finding and verdict shape, per ADR 0123:\n\n- Each finding's `decision`, the key `finalize_verdict`'s partition reads (`orchestrator.py:296-299`), is set from severity alone: `blocker` becomes `\"block\"`; `major`, `minor` and `trivial` become `\"advisory\"` (operator decision on the epic, 2026-11-09). Criterion posture does not change it. Zero blockers is PASS.\n- Field mapping: `title` + `description` become the finding text, `evidence` the evidence list, `suggested_fix` the remediation, `criteria` the criteria list, filtered to ids in `registry.by_id()` (an empty list is valid), `severity` is kept as an attribute; finding ids are minted with `orchestrator.mint_finding_id` (`orchestrator.py:105`) so dedup and prior-concern matching work unchanged.\n- Any non-clean run becomes INDETERMINATE: runner or provider error, timeout, tool-step or iteration limit exhausted, a truncated (`max_tokens`) or refused (`refusal`/`content_filter`) response, or output failing schema validation. It with the same `resolution_class` the pipeline uses for a failed LLM pass, so `attest.sign_plan_review` (`attest.py:113`) refuses to sign it exactly as it refuses a degraded pipeline verdict.\n- Coverage records `engine: \"agentic\"` and the model that ran.\n\nThe adapted verdict then flows through the unchanged post-dispatch path in `_run_plan_review` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py`, after `produce_plan_review_verdict`): Pass-3 floors, advisory cap, sidecar emit and signing. Mapping at the engine boundary, rather than teaching each reader a second shape, is what keeps every downstream reader untouched.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic_verdict.py (new)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic.py (call the adapter)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py (new)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_verdict_schema_parity.py (new: both engines against the same schemas)\n\n## Testing\n\n- Worked example: findings `[{severity: \"blocker\", ...}, {severity: \"major\", ...}]` produce `verdict: BLOCK` with one `blocking` and one `advisory` entry; `[{severity: \"major\"}, {severity: \"trivial\"}]` produce PASS with two advisory entries; `[]` produces PASS with none.\n- Failure/edge: runner error, timeout, limit exhaustion, truncation, refusal and schema-invalid output each produce INDETERMINATE, and a test counts zero attestations written for each; an unknown severity value is treated as advisory and logged, never as blocking by default.\n- Schema parity: a pipeline verdict from `FakeRunner` and an agentic verdict both validate against `plan_review_verdict.schema.json`, and both sidecar payloads validate against `review_result.schema.json`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The severity-to-verdict and field mappings above are pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py`.\n- [ ] Both engines' verdicts and sidecars validate against the same schemas, pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_verdict_schema_parity.py`.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic_verdict.py","reason":"new adapter"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic.py","reason":"call adapter"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py","reason":"mapping tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_verdict_schema_parity.py","reason":"schema parity tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","2473-79b7-1048-4a71"],["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"75af-1212-aa22-463f","ticket_type":"story","title":"Agentic verdict adapter: map agent findings onto the plan_review_verdict and REVIEW_RESULT schemas","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4f151d33-0abd-4a0f-8255-9f3affe54538","9a57c356-a20a-40fa-b981-81fa74203a4d","c64a6c84-2f31-49ab-a0f2-e33321b5db5a","7ea8e375-b1a3-4ad6-9321-3dae241fd5b1","9f3d73e7-7961-4cc7-a801-3ef2896413de"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794262497745566002,"uuid":"8c3f6543-2e93-4c09-9170-988efc2c9716"}